'''Cat Combo''' (にゃんコンボ, ''Nyankonbo'', '''Nyan Combo''' or '''Nyankombo''') is a feature added in the [[Version 4.0 Update]] of [[Nyanko Daisensou]] and [[Version 3.0 Update|Version 3.0]] of [[The Battle Cats]], available after completing Chapter 1 of [[Empire of Cats]]. When using a combination of certain Cats within the first 5 entries (top row) of a slot, additional effects will appear in battle. The Cats do not need to be in a fixed order, and having multiple Combos on the same slot is possible. All discovered Combos can be seen in the Cat Combo List, accessible from the Equip Screen. As of [[Version 16.0 Update|Version 16.0]], Cat Combos can also be unlocked via [[Talents]].

There are also Combos from [[Version 4.7 Update|Version 4.7]] that were eventually removed, most of them having multiple [[:Category:Gacha Cats|gacha units]]. For the removed Combo list, see [[Cat Combo (Version 4.7)]].

'''Combos can still be activated if any units required are in more advanced forms.''' For example, [[Moby Dick (Combo)|Moby Dick]] is activated by [[Fortune Teller Cat (Rare Cat)|Fisherman Cat]], [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Whale Cat]] and [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Whale Cat]], but can also work with Doctor Cat, Island Cat and Manic Island Cat.

Combos are applied separately to [[Treasure]]s. For example, using a Massive Damage Sm Combo with all Treasures maxed will result in the relevant units' damage against their targets being multiplied by 4.4x, rather than 4.1x. Combos with the same effects are applied additively to each other when used together. Unit Attack and Defense Up Combos are applied separately to Strong, Resistant and Massive Damage ones. E.g., pairing [[Scantily Clad (Combo)|Scantily Clad]] with [[Land-Air Assault (Combo)|Land-Air Assault]] would make a Massive Damage unit deal 5.52x damage against their targets instead of just 5.4x.

